  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the iCloud account sync switch in Réglages to have a **short name**, « Synchro des comptes dans iCloud », with its explanation in an **info bubble** instead of a paragraph under the switch, so the section stays compact. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17.)\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SecuritySettingsSections.swift:13`: `Toggle(AccountSyncMessages.title, …)`, with the title « Synchroniser mes comptes via le trousseau iCloud » (`Accounts/AccountsModel+Sync.swift:51`).\n- `SecuritySettingsSections.swift:24`: `Text(AccountSyncMessages.explanation)` under the switch. This is the text the operator reviewed for #312: what travels (cookies and `hash_check`, never a password), end-to-end encryption, and what turning it off does.\n- The old name is cited in `docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md:73`, `docs/LOTS.md:244` and `docs/lots/LOT-173-keychain-sync-lock.md:93`.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Rename the switch to « Synchro des comptes dans iCloud » (`AccountSyncMessages.title`).\n2. Move `AccountSyncMessages.explanation` **verbatim** into an info bubble: an `info.circle` button on the row opens a `.popover` with `presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)`, the same pattern as #1062. The text itself does not change, since the operator reviewed it.\n3. The switch-off reasons (`switchedOff`) and error messages stay where they are, visible under the row when they apply. Only the static explanation moves.\n4. Accessibility: the button's label is « À propos de la synchro des comptes ».\n5. Docs: update the quoted name in LOT-173's spec and in `LOTS.md`. **ADR 0013:73** quotes it too: add a dated amendment line (« renamed … 2026-11-17, #<this issue> ») rather than rewriting the decision. An ADR edit means cloud/orch merges this PR.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A test that the title is the new text and the explanation is unchanged.\n- A view test that the explanation is in the popover, not under the row.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nRéglages: the short title, and a tap on (i) shows the explanation in a bubble.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
